+++ b/README.md
@@ -306,6 +306,20 @@ # ~/.config/plannotator-tui/config.toml
 Without `code_theme` nothing is highlighted, and a fence's opening line shows its backticks
 without the language name.
 
+Fenced `mermaid` blocks are drawn as box-drawing diagrams in the `code-block` colour,
+whether or not `code_theme` is set:
+
+```toml
+[ui]
+mermaid = true   # default; false shows the Mermaid source as plain code
+```
+
+A diagram is drawn once, at the width the document has when it is opened or reloaded; a
+later resize clips it rather than redrawing it. A block that cannot be drawn (a parse error,
+an unsupported diagram type) shows its source instead. A drag anywhere in a diagram selects
+the whole block, and a note on it quotes the Mermaid source, not the drawing. Mermaid
+inside a list or quote is shown as code.
+
 On a wide terminal, `[ui]` can keep the text to a readable measure:
 
 ```toml
