+## 20. Mermaid drawn as text with boxmaid (2026-11-18)
+
+Local patch, not upstream. A top-level fence whose info string starts with `mermaid` is a
+`Diagram` block, drawn by `boxmaid` (pinned `=0.1.1`) as box-drawing text in the
+`code-block` colour; `[ui] mermaid = false` turns it back into plain code. Why boxmaid: its
+output is closest to Pi's own Mermaid renderer, it adds six crates (no C, no JavaScript),
+and its failure mode is harmless here: a block it cannot draw shows its source. Its
+optional `ratatui` feature targets ratatui 0.29 and stays off; the `Picture`'s lines are
+turned into `Text` here. The risk is its youth: one author, a 0.1 version. The exact pin
+makes every upgrade a deliberate one, to be checked with `samples/diagrams.md`.
+
+Glyphs have no source characters, so alignment cannot place them. Every diagram cell maps
+to the block's first byte instead, which lets a note on the block highlight the drawing and
+lets jump-to find it, and a drag that touches a diagram widens to the whole block. A note's
+quote and its rendered `originalText` are both the Mermaid source, never the drawing.
+
+A diagram is drawn once, at the width the layout is built with (open or reload), and clipped
+like code on a resize. Redrawing on reflow would put rendering back on the resize path;
+it can come later if clipping bothers anyone. Mermaid nested in a list or quote is not
+drawn: it is part of that block and shows as code.
+
